  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "hb8w4C117tmzh9WFAjrz454u0e0=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:11.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The two shipped analytics processors partition the metric namespace by prefix, which is what makes `subscribeToSource` and `select` filters composable later.\n\n**Sources** (the `source` field on each series value):\n\n- `DriveAnalyticsProcessor` \u2192 `ph/drive/{documentId}/{branch}/{scope}`\n- `DocumentAnalyticsProcessor` \u2192 `ph/doc/{documentId}/{branch}/{scope}`\n\n**Dimensions on `DriveOperations`** \u2014 four of them:\n\n| Dimension | Path shape |\n| --- | --- |\n| `drive` | `ph/drive/{documentId}/{branch}/{scope}/{revision}` |\n| `operation` | `ph/drive/operation/{actionType}/{operationIndex}` |\n| `target` | `ph/drive/target/{DRIVE\\|NODE}/{targetId}` |\n| `actionType` | `ph/drive/actionType/{CREATED\\|DUPLICATED\\|UPDATED\\|MOVED\\|REMOVED}/{targetId}` |\n\n**Dimensions on `DocumentOperations`** \u2014 only three: `drive` (`ph/doc/drive/...`), `operation` (`ph/doc/operation/...`) and `target` (`ph/doc/target/...`). There is no `actionType`, because a generic document's action names are model-specific and cannot be bucketed into a fixed vocabulary.\n\nTwo things follow from the path design. First, `revision` (the operation index) is baked into the last segment of the `drive` dimension, so an un-truncated query yields one group per operation; you almost always want `lod: { drive: 1 }` to collapse back to per-drive. Second, `targetId` is the last segment of both `target` and `actionType`, so `lod: 1` on those gives you the type only, and full depth gives you per-node breakdowns \u2014 the same dimension serves both questions.\n\n`targetId` resolution for node actions is a fallback chain in the shipped code \u2014 `input.id || input.targetId || input.srcFolder || documentId` \u2014 which is worth knowing when a `MOVE_NODE` row shows the source folder rather than the moved node.\n\nProvenance: draft `04-Reference/04-Processors/_07-DriveAnalyticsHooks.md`; every path template and the dimension counts verified against `packages/shared/processors/drive-analytics/{drive,document}-processor.ts` at 6.2.2-dev.45. The draft's \"Complete Dimensions Reference\" lists four dimensions without noting that only drive metrics carry all four.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:11.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:11.000Z"
    }
  },
